 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "The dashboard's shell store is now made when `bridge.ts` loads, so a shell event published at startup is no longer lost before a page reads the shell.\n\nThe only file changed is `web/src/bridge.ts`:\n- **New function:** `startShellStore()` sits right after `storeOfGlobal()` and returns it. It is called once at module level, right after its definition.\n- **Doc comments:** `shellStore` and `useShell` now say the store is made at start, not at the first `useShell()`.\n\nI reviewed the diff and re-ran the checks myself:\n- `tsc -b` is clean.\n- `pnpm --dir web lint` ran oxlint without errors.\n- `pnpm --dir web test` printed no pass/fail line in the output I looked at. The implementer reported 586 tests passing, including the new `bridge.test.ts` case for an event published before the first store read. I didn't see that count myself.\n\nI didn't run the desktop app. Startup behaviour is checked only by that module-load test, not by watching a real update status arrive.", "ttft_ms": 2174, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 11523, "uuid": "956cca2a-00f1-4cf1-b841-12061923c3d8", "ttft_stream_ms": 1308, "time_to_request_ms": 19, "first_content_frame_ms": 1309, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
